  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FemFocus - SIHA - Combatting Violence Against Women &amp; Supporting WHRDs - Horn of Africa: Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIHA will finance and strengthen in-country partners in the Horn of Africa, specifically in Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, and Uganda. 

The proposed activities are:

Financing: Support for survivor-centered services (legal aid, psychosocial support, emergency assistance, health referrals), WHRD protection measures (digital and physical security, relocation, legal and medical support), and coalition-based advocacy and dialogue.

Capacity strengthening: Ongoing accompaniment on financial management, compliance, monitoring and reporting; technical support on protection pathways, documentation, and accountability; and development of participatory tools and manuals grounded in local practice.

The logic being that IF WROs and WHRDs operating in high-risk contexts have access to financing for survivor centered services AND receive sustained capacity strengthening tailored to their operational 
realities, THEN they will be able to deliver safer, higher-quality VAW/CVAW response services, protect themselves and survivors, document violations, and engage more effectively with accountability and dialogue processes, because locally led actors are best positioned to respond to violence, adapt to rapidly changing contexts, and sustain long-term engagement when institutional, technical, and financial barriers are addressed simultaneously.

Primary target groups include women and girl survivors of VAW, WHRDs, paralegals, and frontline service providers. In-country partners include SIHA member organizations, affiliates, and 
CBO/CSOs with demonstrated engagement in combating VAW, alongside WHRD networks and Cooperatives. Key stakeholders also include justice, protection, and accountability actors at local, national, and regional levels.</narrative>
  </description>
